## 14. ANIMATION AND INTERACTION ENGINE

Build a coherent motion system rather than adding unrelated animations to every element.

### Required motion features

Where appropriate, implement:

- Page-load entrance transitions.
- Smooth section reveals.
- Staggered card animations.
- Subtle parallax.
- Navigation transitions.
- Button hover animations.
- Animated background gradients.
- Refined accordion transitions.
- Responsive mobile menu transitions.
- Interactive service cards.
- Subtle counter animations.
- Fluid transitions between visual states.

Use CSS transitions and keyframes for simple effects.

Use IntersectionObserver for viewport-based animations.

Use requestAnimationFrame for custom continuous animation when appropriate.

Use a specialist animation library only if it materially improves the result and can be included and deployed reliably.

Avoid loading multiple large animation libraries unnecessarily.

### Performance requirements

Animations must not make the site feel slow.

Prefer transform and opacity animations over repeatedly animating expensive layout properties.

Avoid unnecessarily animating large full-screen filters.

Do not continuously recalculate layout on every scroll event.

Avoid excessive DOM elements and expensive mouse-tracking effects.

Do not make the page wait for decorative animations before displaying important content.

### Accessibility requirements

Respect the prefers-reduced-motion media query.

When reduced motion is enabled:

- Disable unnecessary parallax.
- Reduce or remove decorative movement.
- Avoid large spatial transitions.
- Keep content immediately accessible.
- Preserve all essential functionality.

All interactions must work without requiring a mouse.

